      "message": "fix(post): state the rotary return after a tilted section\n\nThe Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts kept the lean of a tilted section into\nthe next section. The angle words are modal, the tilted exit keeps its\npose, and endPreamble reset only the script's memory. A 3-axis section\nafter it states no angles, so it cut with the axes still tilted.\n\nAt each section start, after the G49 line and before the tool change,\nuprightAfterTilt() reads the angles the control holds (rotAt). A rotary\naway from zero is commanded back with G00 <letter>0 after a retract to\nthe reference height. The first X/Y traverse then states its height\nagain. Doosan unclamps and clamps a turning A around the return.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/upright_after_tilt.rs (Fanuc and Doosan on\ntilthead.mch with the same tool and a tool change, Tormach PathPilot on\nan A-axis machine, and an upright program that writes no return).\n\nStacked on #3421. Item 3 of the issue (an app refusal for a user's post\nscript) is #3477.\n\nFixes #3466\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
